      "writtenOn": "2023-05-05T19:44:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "William: adding the line `sdev-\u003ebroken_fua \u003d 1;` is safe because that causes the SCSI disk driver to submit a SYNCHRONIZE CACHE command if the filesystem sets REQ_FUA instead of setting the FUA bit in WRITE commands. From a functional point of view, both are equivalent.\n\nJaegeuk: I think the upstream kernel community rejected patch [2]?\n\nI propose that we proceed with adding `sdev-\u003ebroken_fua \u003d 1;` because all UFS devices we know of perform better with that line added.",
      "parentUuid": "154d85f3_9d3c3d03",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 5107,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 5107,
        "endChar": 40
